{
  "contract": "llm-audit-single",
  "version": 1,
  "description": "A single call in the transcript audit store (RFC-0015 in mercury-composable). mercury-python and mercury-nodejs ship this file byte-identical and run every case against their own fake of the Anthropic SDK, with the memory working store and the reference audit store. A case names the route, the config keys in force, the headers and the trace of the call (trace_id and trace_path; none: the call runs outside a trace), the request body and what the fake provider does - provider kinds as in llm-helper-vectors.json, with content as the assistant's blocks exactly as the API returned them. The expectation is what the caller receives (a subset of the reply map, the stream's frames, or the error) and the two rows the audit store holds once the call's saves and the function's mailbox are idle - or null for both when nothing is recorded, in which case no event was sent and no record saved. A row lists every column but the ones a run decides: the harness checks that conversation is the same 32 hexadecimal reference in both rows, that started_at and ended_at are ISO-8601 UTC stamps with milliseconds, equal in both rows and in order, that updated_at is such a stamp, and that expires_at is started_at plus expires_after_s. When rows are expected, exactly one event was sent, {conversation, check: true}, and the working record is gone after the check.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "single/a-call-is-a-conversation-of-one-turn",
      "route": "llm.chat",
      "config": {
        "llm.transcript.store": "memory",
        "llm.transcript.audit": "postgres",
        "llm.transcript.audit.single": "true"
      },
      "headers": {
        "x-graph-id": "ticket-triage",
        "x-node": "classify",
        "my_correlation_id": "corr-41"
      },
      "trace": {
        "trace_id": "5a1c5a1c5a1c5a1c5a1c5a1c5a1c5a1c",
        "trace_path": "POST /api/graph/ticket-triage"
      },
      "body": {
        "prompt": "The app crashes when I upload a file",
        "system": "You label tickets."
      },
      "provider": {
        "kind": "message",
        "model": "claude-opus-5-5",
        "stop_reason": "end_turn",
        "deltas": [
          "bug"
        ],
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "bug"
          }
        ],
        "usage": {
          "input_tokens": 120,
          "output_tokens": 9
        },
        "request_id": "req_single_1"
      },
      "expect": {
